IMPORT prelude

-- National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library. Dates are compared by serial.
--
-- A period of months "starting on" a day (s 34(6), s 40(1)) is read with the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2G
-- (borrowed, not deposited): it includes that day and ends immediately before the corresponding day in the later month,
-- or at the end of that month if it has no corresponding day. A period of weeks or days "beginning on" or "starting on"
-- the date of a notice (s 24(4), s 34(6)) includes that date, so 4 weeks from 2 March end on 29 March.
-- A last day on a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday is NOT moved (Acts Interpretation Act s 36(2)); see NOTES.md, fork F9.
--
-- Sourced from the Federal Register of Legislation, Commonwealth of Australia, CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the National Redress Scheme Act 2018`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- The day a given number of plain days after a day (a negative number goes back).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` a `is after` b IF DATE_SERIAL a GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` a `is before` b IF DATE_SERIAL a LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` a `is on or before` b IF DATE_SERIAL a AT MOST DATE_SERIAL b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` a `is on or after` b IF DATE_SERIAL a AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL b

-- The number of days in a calendar month (the first of the next month, less the first of this month).
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the length of month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The month count of a day (years times 12, plus the month less one), so that months can be added and taken away.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month count of` d MEANS (DATE_YEAR d TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH d MINUS 1)

GIVEN c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year of month count` c MEANS FLOOR (c DIVIDED BY 12)

GIVEN c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month of month count` c MEANS (c MINUS (`the year of month count` c TIMES 12)) PLUS 1

-- The day with the same day-number n months on (n may be negative); where the later month has no such day, its last day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the same day` n `months on from` d MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY d AT MOST `the length of month` `tm` `of` `ty`
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY d) `tm` `ty`
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (`the length of month` `tm` `of` `ty`) `tm` `ty`
    WHERE
        `tc` MEANS `the month count of` d PLUS n
        `tm` MEANS `the month of month count` `tc`
        `ty` MEANS `the year of month count` `tc`

-- The last day of a period of n months starting on (and including) a day: Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2G. The period
-- ends immediately before the corresponding day n months on; if that month has no corresponding day, at its end.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the first day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the` n `month period starting on` `the first day` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY `the first day` AT MOST `the length of month` `tm` `of` `ty`
    THEN `the date` (0 MINUS 1) `days after` (DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY `the first day`) `tm` `ty`)
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (`the length of month` `tm` `of` `ty`) `tm` `ty`
    WHERE
        `tc` MEANS `the month count of` `the first day` PLUS n
        `tm` MEANS `the month of month count` `tc`
        `ty` MEANS `the year of month count` `tc`

-- The anniversary k years after a day. A 29 February has no anniversary in a year that is not a leap year: the
-- anniversary is then taken as 1 March (fork F8 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN k IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the anniversary` k `years after` d MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 2 AND DATE_DAY d EQUALS 29 AND `the length of month` 2 `of` (DATE_YEAR d PLUS k) EQUALS 28
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 (DATE_YEAR d PLUS k)
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY d) (DATE_MONTH d) (DATE_YEAR d PLUS k)

-- s 6: "child means a person under the age of 18". A person turns 18 on the 18th anniversary of their birth.
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day I turn 18` `my date of birth` MEANS `the anniversary` 18 `years after` `my date of birth`

-- The number of whole years from one day to a later day (s 30(2) step 4, s 30(4) step 1: "the number of whole years").
GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the whole years from` a `to` b MEANS
    IF `the day` b `is before` a
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the day` b `is before` (`the anniversary` `the raw count` `years after` a)
         THEN `the raw count` MINUS 1
         ELSE `the raw count`
    WHERE
        `the raw count` MEANS DATE_YEAR b MINUS DATE_YEAR a

-- s 6: "scheme start day means the day this Act commences." Section 2, table item 1: 1 July 2018 if Royal Assent came
-- before 1 July 2018; column 3 says "1 July 2018 (paragraph (a) applies)". Column 3 is not part of the Act (s 2(2)):
-- see NOTES.md, finding 1.
`the scheme start day` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2018

-- s 193(1): the Act "ceases to have effect at the end of the day (the scheme sunset day) that is: (a) the tenth
-- anniversary of the scheme start day; or (b) if, before the tenth anniversary, the rules prescribe a day that is after the
-- tenth anniversary--that day." The deposited Rules (Compilation No. 9, 19 February 2025) prescribe no later day.
`the scheme sunset day` MEANS `the anniversary` 10 `years after` `the scheme start day`
